course: dictionary
lesson: 14901
title: Straight-line words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Rectilinear is a long word, but it is built from parts you may know. Rect comes from a Latin word for straight, and linear is about lines. So rectilinear means made of straight lines. «The garden is a rectilinear shape with four square corners.» The garden has only straight sides, so it is rectilinear.
explain: Look at the words around it to check. «The tiles on the floor make a rectilinear pattern of squares and rectangles.» A square has straight sides and no curves, so the pattern has only straight lines. If a shape has a round edge or a curve, it is not rectilinear.
explain: In maths, rectilinear shapes are often made from rectangles. «Find the area of this rectilinear shape.» Split the shape into rectangles, work out each area, and add them together. In science, «rectilinear motion» means moving in a straight line, like a ball rolling straight across the floor.
fact: Rectilinear means made of straight lines, or moving in a straight line.
fact: «Rectilinear» is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like «rectilinear shape» or «rectilinear figure».
fact: A rectilinear shape has only straight sides, often with right angles, like a rectangle or an L-shape.
fact: «Rectilinear motion» is movement in a straight line, as in «The toy car moved in rectilinear motion across the table.»
fact: The word is built from parts: rect (straight, from Latin) and linear (about lines). Knowing the parts helps you work out the meaning.
exercise: «The garden is a rectilinear shape with four square corners.» What does rectilinear mean here? | Very large | Made of curved lines | Full of water | *Made of straight lines
exercise: «The tiles make a rectilinear pattern of squares.» Which shape is rectilinear? | A bubble | *An L-shape | A circle | A wheel
exercise: «The toy car moved in rectilinear motion across the table.» What does rectilinear motion mean? | Not moving at all | *Moving in a straight line | Moving up and down | Moving in circles
exercise: Maya says rectilinear sounds like rectangle. Which word is the best clue to its meaning? | Shape, because it is a shape | Angle, which is a number | *Linear, which is about lines | Rectilinear, which is about recta
test: «To find the area of this rectilinear shape, split it into two rectangles.» What should you do first? | Add the sides together | *Split the shape into rectangles | Count the corners only | Draw a circle around it
test: Which of these is NOT rectilinear? | *A shape with a curved edge like a circle | A square | An L-shape | A rectangle
exam: «The path was rectilinear, going straight across the park with no bends.» What does rectilinear suggest about the path? | *It has no bends and goes in straight lines | It curves around the trees | It goes up a hill | It is covered in water
